id: pmc-6jr4
title: Enforce a real coverage gate by running tests against TypeScript sources
description: "The package measured no coverage at all: tests imported the compiled output from dist, so the only obtainable numbers pointed at generated JavaScript offsets an author cannot act on, and no threshold was wired into any gate. The suite now runs against the TypeScript sources directly. Node executes TypeScript natively from the version floor this package already declares, so tests import source modules and the CLI subprocess tests spawn the source entrypoint, which puts the coverage report on real source lines. Enabling rewriteRelativeImportExtensions lets a source file import its siblings by TypeScript extension while tsc still emits the JavaScript specifier into dist, so the published artifact is byte-identical in shape. The gate is scripts/coverage-gate.ts: it enforces per-dimension thresholds and reconciles the reported file list against a walk of the source tree. That second check is the point. Node omits files that never load from its report entirely rather than reporting them at zero, so without it a package can satisfy a full threshold while an entire module goes unexercised."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: code-quality,coverage,testing
created_at: "2026-07-28T23:14:26.924Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T01:34:01.805Z"
deadline: "2026-08-05T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T23:14:51.370Z"
author: claude-code
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Tests import TypeScript sources rather than dist so coverage reports on editable lines; the gate fails the build when any threshold regresses; the gate fails when a source file never loads, proven by a negative control; thresholds are recorded in package.json as a ratchet at the measured baseline; the gate runs in the release check and in CI on Node 22 and 26."
resolution: "Tests moved onto TypeScript sources and scripts/coverage-gate.ts wired into release:check and CI."
expected_result: "A coverage gate runs in the release check and in CI on both supported Node lines, reports against TypeScript sources, and fails when a source file is untested or a threshold regresses."
actual_result: "npm run check passes. npm run coverage passes with 192 tests, all seven source files present in the report, at 89.83 line, 79.24 branch and 90.71 function coverage. A negative control adding an untested src file made the gate exit 1 and name that file, so the presence check is not vacuous. Thresholds pinned at 89/79/90."
