comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:14:26.924Z",claude-code,"Negative control run: adding an untested src file made the gate exit 1 and name the file,so the presence check is not vacuous."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:14:26.924Z",claude-code,Do not rewrite the node_modules pm-cli dist path when converting test spawn targets; only the package's own dist references become source paths.
  "2026-07-28T23:24:44.297Z",claude-code,"CI measured 78.96 branch coverage where this host measured 79.24. Cause: src/release-context.ts extractOffset branches on whether a timestamp carries a UTC offset, so a host in a non-UTC zone takes a path CI does not. The gate now pins TZ=UTC when it spawns the runner, which makes the measurement identical on any machine, and the thresholds are set from that reproducible number: 89 line, 78 branch, 90 function. First concrete target for the follow-up to 100 is release-context.ts line 447."
  "2026-07-29T01:34:01.803Z",claude-code,"Reconciliation of the numbers on this item, since three appear in the record. The figures in the description and actual_result (89.83 line, 79.24 branch, 90.71 function) were measured on this host before the gate pinned TZ, and are not reproducible elsewhere. The authoritative baseline is the TZ-normalized one: 89.81 line, 78.96 branch, 90.71 function, which this host and CI now both produce. The enforced thresholds in package.json are 89/78/90, floored from that. Where this item still shows the pre-normalization numbers, the note history is the correction; the closed record is not rewritten because these trackers are append-only and history-audited."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:14:26.924Z",claude-code,"Node omits never-loaded files from its coverage report rather than reporting them at zero,so a threshold flag alone is satisfiable by narrowing what the suite imports. Any coverage gate must reconcile the report against the source tree."
